    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the incremental level rules with a points system, exposing both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n\n**`MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 rewrote the computation:\n- `points(owner, repo)`: starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure over 365 days.\n- `level(points)`: bands points \u2192 `1` (0-1), `2` (2-3), `3` (4-5), `4` (6+).\n- `of(...)` now returns `level(points(...))`, keeping existing callers working.\n- The old `isSoleHouseholdMember` check became `householdSize(...) >= 3`, counting this owner plus earlier owners (lower id) sharing its `householdId` \u2014 a no-postcode owner is a household of one. This preserves the \"fixed at creation\" semantics.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field (integer, min 0, readOnly) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it, and updated both field descriptions to document the new rules.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints(owner)` helper and a `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints`, alongside the existing `membershipLevel` mapping.\n\nThe acceptance test's case (email + unique name + single-member household + zero tenure) now scores 3 points \u2192 level 2, exactly as the test expects. Note the only `@Test` in the repo is `AcceptanceTest`; the full `mvn test` run passed.",
