    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered list of everything applied to `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. The caller must hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before the pipeline runs.\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `ValidateOwner` (not transactional)\n\nBinds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` and, in this order:\n\n1. **First name** required \u2014 non-blank, else added to missing list.\n2. **Last name** required \u2014 non-blank.\n3. **Address normalized** (`AddressNormalizer.normalize`) *in place*, **then** required \u2014 rejected if blank only after normalization. (side-effect: mutates/stores normalized address)\n4. **City** required \u2014 non-blank.\n5. **Telephone** required \u2014 non-blank.\n6. If any of the above are missing \u2192 **`MissingOwnerFieldsException`** (400, lists offending fields).\n7. **Telephone normalized to E.164** (`TelephoneE164.normalize`); if it can't form a valid number \u2192 **`InvalidTelephoneException`** (400). (side-effect: stores normalized telephone)\n8. **Email** (optional): if present, trimmed + **lower-cased**; must match the email regex else **`InvalidEmailException`** (400); its domain must not be in the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) else **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** (400). (side-effect: stores lower-cased email)\n9. **Postcode** (optional): if present, trimmed; must be exactly 4 digits else **`InvalidPostcodeException`** (400); if the city maps to a known region (`CityRegion.postcodeRangeOf`), the value must fall within that region's numeric range else **`InvalidPostcodeException`** (400). (side-effect: stores trimmed postcode)\n10. Publishes the validated/normalized body as `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`.\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `CheckIdentityUnique` (transactional)\n\nScans **all** existing owners:\n- **Exact-identity duplicate** \u2014 `telephone|email|householdId` key (`OwnerIdentity`) equals an existing owner's \u2192 **`DuplicateIdentityException`** (409). Always enforced.\n- **Household duplicate** \u2014 same `householdId` (derived from `lastName + postcode`) as an existing owner \u2192 **`DuplicateIdentityException`** (409), **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, which bypasses this rule. An owner with no postcode has no household, so only the exact-identity rule applies.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `CheckCityCapacity` (transactional)\n\nCounts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, trimmed). If **\u2265 50** (`MAX_PER_CITY`) \u2192 **`CityAtCapacityException`** (409).\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `ResolveRegistrationDate` (not transactional)\n\n- Effective date = supplied `registrationDate`, or **server's current date** if none.\n- A supplied date **later than today** \u2192 **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (400); back-dating allowed.\n- If the effective date is **Saturday/Sunday, rolls forward to Monday**.\n- Publishes the adjusted `Out<LocalDate>` (side-effect: this business-day-adjusted date drives the daily-limit count, the stored `registrationDate`, and the membership-number year).\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `CheckDailyLimit` (transactional)\n\nCounts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the adjusted date. If **\u2265 100** (`MAX_PER_DAY`) \u2192 **`DailyLimitExceededException`** (429).\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `BuildOwner` (transactional)\n\nMaps DTO \u2192 `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`, and **overrides** `registrationDate` with the adjusted business-day date. Publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `AssignHousehold` (transactional)\n\nSets `householdId` = first 12 upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized `(lastName, postcode)`. Owner with no postcode is left with no household id. (side-effect on entity)\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode` (transactional)\n\nSets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION comes from city/postcode (`CityRegion.localityOf`) and HASH8 is first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`. (side-effect on entity)\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` (transactional)\n\nSets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the (adjusted) registration year. (side-effect on entity)\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `AssignNamesakeCount` (transactional)\n\nCounts pre-existing owners sharing this owner's first+last name (case-insensitive) \u2014 excludes the not-yet-saved new owner \u2014 and stores it as `namesakeCount`. (side-effect on entity)\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `SaveOwner` (transactional)\n\n`ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 **persists** the owner (assigns its id).\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` (transactional)\n\nEmits an `AUDIT` log line with the new id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel` (`MembershipLevel.of`). (side-effect: audit log)\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (transactional)\n\nMaps to `OwnerDto` and enriches the response: sets `bulkSignupWarning` (`BulkSignup.warningFor`), and `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (null when the owner is a declared household member via `sharesHousehold`, otherwise from `PossibleDuplicate.matchFor`). Sends **`201 Created`** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Notes**\n- Steps 2 onward all run under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so persistence commits **once at the end** of the pipeline; `ValidateOwner` and `ResolveRegistrationDate` are the only non-transactional steps.\n- Validation ordering is deliberate: missing-field/format checks (400) precede uniqueness/capacity checks (409) which precede the daily-limit check (429), and date resolution precedes the daily-limit count so both use the same adjusted business day."
